14. Decision Is Not Knowledge

MOS SHALL distinguish:

Observation

=

Something happened


Fact

=

Something believed to be true


Decision

=

Something chosen to do

A Decision SHALL NOT automatically become a Fact.

15. Commitment Model

A Decision creates a Commitment.

Commitment represents:

The intention to execute a chosen cognitive action.

Commitments connect:

Decision

↓

Plan

↓

Capability

↓

Execution
16. Delegation Model

Intent and Decisions MAY be delegated.

Example:

Human Intent

↓

Agent Decision

↓

Specialized Agent Capability

↓

Execution

Delegation SHALL preserve:

ownership
authority
provenance
responsibility
17. Multi-Agent Intent Coordination

Multiple agents MAY participate in shared Intent.

Coordination requires:

Intent identity
ownership model
authority boundaries
conflict handling

Agents SHALL NOT silently override another agent's Intent.

18. Intent Conflict Resolution

Conflicting Intents SHALL be resolved through explicit policies.

Resolution MAY consider:

priority
authority
resources
constraints
expected outcomes

Conflict resolution SHALL produce an explainable Decision.

19. Decision Policies

Decision policies are Meta-Cognitive Elements.

Examples:

Reliability Policy

Prefer safer outcomes.

Efficiency Policy

Prefer lower resource usage.

Accuracy Policy

Prefer higher confidence.

Cost Policy

Prefer cheaper solutions.

Policies SHALL be versioned and explainable according to RFC-0004.

20. Evaluation Model

Every Decision SHOULD define evaluation criteria.

Evaluation determines:

success
failure
unexpected outcomes
future improvement

Evaluation results become new Cognitive Elements.

21. Reflection Loop

After execution:

Decision

↓

Outcome

↓

Evaluation

↓

Reflection

↓

Learning

↓

Improved Decision Model

This creates continuous cognitive improvement.

22. Explainability Requirements

Every Decision SHALL be explainable.

The system SHALL be able to answer:

Why was this decision created?
Which Intent caused it?
Which alternatives existed?
Which policies influenced it?
Which assumptions were made?
Why was this option selected?
What happened afterwards?
